The Oracle connection string builder in `ConnectionInfo.cs` documents that non-SYS administrative users need specific system privileges (CREATE USER, GRANT ANY PRIVILEGE, etc.), but doesn't explicitly warn that these users cannot use SYSDBA privilege and will encounter ORA-01031 errors without proper grants.

## Changes

- Added explicit WARNING block in `BuildOracleConnectionString()` clarifying that non-SYS users (SYSTEM, custom DBAs) cannot use SYSDBA privilege
- Documented that only SYS user can connect with SYSDBA
- Emphasized that non-SYS accounts must have required system privileges explicitly granted or will fail with ORA-01031

```csharp
// WARNING: Non-SYS users CANNOT use SYSDBA privilege. Only the SYS user can connect with
// SYSDBA privilege. If using a non-SYS administrative account (e.g., SYSTEM or custom DBA),
// that account MUST have the system privileges listed above explicitly granted to it.
// Attempting to use SYSDBA with non-SYS users or lacking required privileges will result
// in ORA-01031 (insufficient privileges) errors during database/user creation operations.
```

This prevents confusion about why database/user creation fails when using administrative accounts other than SYS.

