Completes the Angular Signals migration started in PR #10. Five components (Photos, Rewards, Meals, Lists, Dashboard) were still using RxJS subscriptions and direct backend calls instead of the Signal-based state management pattern.

## Changes

### Component Layer
- Migrated to `inject()` function for dependency injection
- Replaced component properties with signal references from state services
- Converted local UI state to signals (e.g., `showForm = signal(false)`)
- Replaced RxJS subscriptions with async/await pattern using API services
- Updated state mutations to call state service methods

**Before:**
```typescript
export class PhotosComponent implements OnInit {
  photos: Photo[] = [];
  isLoading = false;

  constructor(private photoService: PhotoService) {}

  loadPhotos() {
    this.photoService.getAllPhotos().subscribe({
      next: (photos) => {
        this.photos = photos;
        this.isLoading = false;
      }
    });
  }
}
```

**After:**
```typescript
export class PhotosComponent implements OnInit {
  private photosState = inject(PhotosStateService);
  private photosApi = inject(PhotosApiService);

  readonly photos = this.photosState.sortedPhotos;
  readonly loading = this.photosState.loading;

  async loadPhotos() {
    this.photosState.setLoading(true);
    try {
      const photos = await this.photosApi.getAllPhotos();
      this.photosState.setPhotos(photos);
    } finally {
      this.photosState.setLoading(false);
    }
  }
}
```

### Template Layer
- Replaced `*ngIf` with `@if` control flow
- Replaced `*ngFor` with `@for` with track expressions
- Updated all data access to use signal invocation syntax `()`

**Before:**
```html
<div *ngIf="isLoading">Loading...</div>
<div *ngFor="let photo of photos" class="photo-card">
  <img [src]="photo.filePath">
</div>
```

**After:**
```html
@if (loading()) {
  <div>Loading...</div>
}
@for (photo of photos(); track photo.id) {
  <div class="photo-card">
    <img [src]="photo.filePath">
  </div>
}
```

### API Service Layer
- Created `DashboardApiService` to complete the API wrapper layer
- All API services convert RxJS Observables to Promises using `firstValueFrom()`

## Architecture

Establishes consistent 3-layer pattern across entire application:

```
Component → State Service (Signals) → API Service (Promises) → Backend Service (RxJS)
```

State services (already existed) provide:
- Private writable signals for state
- Public readonly signal accessors
- Computed signals for derived values
- State mutation methods

## Impact

- Fine-grained reactivity: only affected components re-render on state changes
- Reduced Zone.js overhead
- Centralized state management for all features
- Consistent patterns across codebase

