## Overview
Complete the Angular Signals migration that was started but left incomplete. Currently, only CalendarComponent and TasksComponent are using the Signal-based state management pattern, while the remaining components (Photos, Rewards, Meals, Lists, Dashboard) are still calling backend services directly with RxJS subscriptions. This PR will complete the migration to establish a consistent 3-layer architecture across the entire application.

## Current Problem

### Components NOT Using Signals Properly
Based on the code analysis, these components are still using the old pattern:

1. **PhotosComponent** - Using RxJS subscribe, plain arrays, no state service
2. **RewardsComponent** - Calling backend directly
3. **MealsComponent** - Not using state management
4. **ListsComponent** - Missing state service integration
5. **DashboardComponent** - Not leveraging signals

### What's Wrong with Current Implementation

**PhotosComponent Example (Current - INCORRECT):**
```typescript
export class PhotosComponent {
  photos: Photo[] = [];  // ❌ Plain property, not reactive
  isLoading = false;     // ❌ Not a signal

  constructor(
    private photoService: PhotoService  // ❌ Calling backend directly
  ) {}

  loadPhotos() {
    this.photoService.getAllPhotos().subscribe({  // ❌ RxJS subscribe in component
      next: (photos) => {
        this.photos = photos;  // ❌ Direct mutation, no state management
      }
    });
  }
}
```

**Why This is Bad:**
- No centralized state management
- Direct backend service calls from components
- Mixed reactive patterns (some signals, some not)
- Poor performance (no fine-grained reactivity)
- Hard to debug and test
- Inconsistent architecture across the app

## Goal: Consistent 3-Layer Architecture

Implement this pattern everywhere:

```
Component → State Service → API Service → Backend
```

**Each layer has a specific responsibility:**
- **Component**: Display logic, user interactions, delegates to state service
- **State Service**: Holds application state as signals, computed values, business logic
- **API Service**: HTTP calls wrapped as Promises, no business logic
- **Backend**: REST API endpoints

## Implementation Plan

### 1. Create Missing State Services

Create Signal-based state services for remaining features:

**frontend/src/app/services/state/photos-state.service.ts**
```typescript
import { Injectable, signal, computed } from '@angular/core';
import { Photo } from '../../models/photo.model';

@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class PhotosStateService {
  // Private writable signals
  private _photos = signal<Photo[]>([]);
  private _loading = signal(false);
  private _error = signal<string | null>(null);
  private _selectedPhoto = signal<Photo | null>(null);
  private _filter = signal<'all' | 'user' | 'event'>('all');
  private _filterValue = signal<number | null>(null);

  // Public readonly signals
  readonly photos = this._photos.asReadonly();
  readonly loading = this._loading.asReadonly();
  readonly error = this._error.asReadonly();
  readonly selectedPhoto = this._selectedPhoto.asReadonly();

  // Computed signals
  readonly filteredPhotos = computed(() => {
    const photos = this._photos();
    const filter = this._filter();
    const filterValue = this._filterValue();

    if (filter === 'all' || !filterValue) return photos;
    if (filter === 'user') return photos.filter(p => p.uploadedBy === filterValue);
    if (filter === 'event') return photos.filter(p => p.eventId === filterValue);
    return photos;
  });

  readonly photoCount = computed(() => this._photos().length);

  readonly hasPhotos = computed(() => this._photos().length > 0);

  // Methods
  setPhotos(photos: Photo[]) {
    this._photos.set(photos);
  }

  addPhoto(photo: Photo) {
    this._photos.update(photos => [photo, ...photos]);
  }

  updatePhoto(id: number, updates: Partial<Photo>) {
    this._photos.update(photos =>
      photos.map(p => p.id === id ? { ...p, ...updates } : p)
    );
  }

  removePhoto(id: number) {
    this._photos.update(photos => photos.filter(p => p.id !== id));
  }

  setSelectedPhoto(photo: Photo | null) {
    this._selectedPhoto.set(photo);
  }

  setFilter(filter: 'all' | 'user' | 'event', value?: number) {
    this._filter.set(filter);
    this._filterValue.set(value || null);
  }

  setLoading(loading: boolean) {
    this._loading.set(loading);
  }

  setError(error: string | null) {
    this._error.set(error);
  }

  reset() {
    this._photos.set([]);
    this._selectedPhoto.set(null);
    this._filter.set('all');
    this._filterValue.set(null);
    this._loading.set(false);
    this._error.set(null);
